# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the vulnerability is a registry ImagePath (unquoted service path) on a
#     planted service - a config weakness, not a foreground process;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the vulnerable service registration is ALREADY
# present, so a fix must quote the ImagePath (and/or remove the hijack binary);
# no process runs as PID 1 that a restart could kill.
